    "description": "MIC-50-90 bounds minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC) distributions from incomplete antimicrobial susceptibility reports. From MIC50, MIC90, the observed range and exact or rounded counts, it computes the smallest and largest count the report allows in every MIC category and range, names the count that would narrow an open question most, selects the counts a laboratory can publish so that readers can check its conclusions, and gives optional population bounds under stated sampling assumptions. It is available as a Python package, a command-line program, a container image and three Galaxy tools.",
